    "Para ordenar fracciones, observamos cuál representa una parte más pequeña o más grande del todo.\n\n## De menor a mayor\nEmpezamos por la fracción más pequeña y terminamos en la más grande.\n\n**1/4 < 1/2 < 3/4**\n<div class=\"flex items-center gap-2 my-4\">\n  <div class=\"relative w-12 h-12 rounded-full border-2 border-gray-300\" style=\"background: conic-gradient(#3b82f6 0% 25%, #f1f5f9 25% 100%); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: bold; color: #475569;\">1/4</div>\n  <span class=\"text-xl font-bold text-gray-500\"><</span>\n  <div class=\"relative w-12 h-12 rounded-full border-2 border-gray-300\" style=\"background: conic-gradient(#3b82f6 0% 50%, #f1f5f9 50% 100%); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: bold; color: #475569;\">1/2</div>\n  <span class=\"text-xl font-bold text-gray-500\"><</span>\n  <div class=\"relative w-12 h-12 rounded-full border-2 border-gray-300\" style=\"background: conic-gradient(#3b82f6 0% 75%, #f1f5f9 75% 100%); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: bold; color: #475569;\">3/4</div>\n</div>",
